\f0\fs24 \cf0 PROJECT: MOTIONVITALS AI\
Turning Physical Function into Actionable Clinical Evidence\
\
CONTEXT\
\
We are developing MotionVitals AI for the 2026 ExecuTorch\
Hackathon, sponsored by Qualcomm, Meta, GitHub, and others.\
\
This project should be presented as an early-stage healthcare\
technology company with a credible commercialization strategy,\
not simply a computer vision demonstration.\
\
We need to produce four interconnected deliverables:\
\
1. Comprehensive product and business concept\
2. Investor-style / hackathon pitch deck\
3. Technical product and engineering specifications\
4. Market adoption, validation, and commercialization roadmap\
\
All four must tell one consistent story.\
\
Use the materials I provide as background, consolidate\
overlapping concepts, and identify contradictions or unsupported\
claims.\
\
Do not invent clinical evidence, performance results, regulatory\
approvals, market sizes, competitor prices, or cost savings.\
\
Use credible public sources and maintain a reference list.\
\
--------------------------------------------------\
1. PRODUCT DEFINITION AND BUSINESS PROBLEM\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
Create a comprehensive project document.\
\
Working name:\
MotionVitals AI\
\
Tagline:\
Turning Physical Function into Actionable Clinical Evidence\
\
CORE BUSINESS PROBLEM\
\
In pharmaceutical development, demonstrating a biological\
effect does not necessarily demonstrate a meaningful\
functional benefit to patients.\
\
Sponsors use physical performance assessments, clinical\
outcome assessments, patient-reported outcomes, imaging,\
and biological biomarkers to characterize treatment effects.\
\
However, some physical-function assessments require trained\
personnel, manual timing or scoring, standardized equipment,\
and repeated visits.\
\
Potential challenges include:\
\
- Variability across assessors and clinical sites\
- Staff time required for test administration and scoring\
- Incomplete or inconsistent measurements\
- Difficulty comparing longitudinal assessments\
- Limited integration of functional data with biomarkers\
- Cost and operational burden of endpoint collection\
- Limited availability of assessments outside research sites\
\
These are potential problems to validate, not universal\
limitations of existing methods.\
\
OUR PROPOSED SOLUTION\
\
Develop an AI-powered platform that converts standardized\
physical performance assessments into objective,\
reproducible digital clinical measurements.\
\
The platform uses camera-based movement analysis and\
on-device inference to automate relevant portions of\
functional assessments.\
\
Initial supported assessment:\
\
Five-Times Sit-to-Stand (5xSTS).\
\
Future assessments may include:\
\
- 30-second chair stand\
- Timed Up and Go\
- Gait speed\
- Short Physical Performance Battery\
- Selected disease-specific motor assessments\
\
The initial system should produce:\
\
- Repetition count\
- Total completion time\
- Individual movement transition times, if feasible\
- Measurement quality indicators\
- Structured assessment results\
- Longitudinal comparisons\
- Data suitable for export and subsequent clinical analysis\
\
Distinguish established clinical performance measures from\
exploratory camera-derived measurements.\
\
Do not claim the prototype produces validated digital\
biomarkers, diagnoses diseases, or establishes drug efficacy.\
\
