6. TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
Available hackathon hardware:\
\
- Qualcomm Snapdragon X Elite laptop\
- Orbbec Astra 2 depth camera\
- Meta ExecuTorch framework\
\
We do not have an Arduino board or robotic actuators.\
\
COMPUTE TRACK REQUIREMENTS\
\
The implementation must demonstrate genuine\
ExecuTorch model inference on the Snapdragon device.\
\
Prioritize a reliable local inference pipeline.\
\
Proposed architecture:\
\
CAMERA INPUT\
    \uc0\u8595 \
POSE ESTIMATION / MOVEMENT DETECTION\
    \uc0\u8595 \
PYTORCH MODEL EXPORTED TO EXECUTORCH\
    \uc0\u8595 \
MOVEMENT EVENT DETECTION\
    \uc0\u8595 \
DETERMINISTIC TEST SCORING\
    \uc0\u8595 \
MEASUREMENT QUALITY CONTROL\
    \uc0\u8595 \
STRUCTURED CLINICAL DATA\
    \uc0\u8595 \
FUNCTIONAL ASSESSMENT DASHBOARD\
\
The engineering team should verify:\
\
- Model compatibility with ExecuTorch\
- Actual .pte model execution\
- Windows ARM64 runtime compatibility\
- Qualcomm acceleration availability\
- Camera SDK compatibility\
- Inference latency\
- Measurement repeatability\
\
Do not assume that ExecuTorch automatically uses\
the Qualcomm NPU.\
\
A CPU fallback is acceptable for technical continuity,\
but must be identified accurately.\
\
Camera compatibility is an important technical risk.\
\
The Orbbec SDK's documented Windows support\
does not establish compatibility with every\
Snapdragon ARM64 configuration.\
\
Prepare standard webcam or prerecorded-video fallbacks.\
\
All model-generated measurements must be labeled\
as experimental until validated.\
