7. HACKATHON MINIMUM VIABLE PRODUCT\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
Build around ONE primary assessment:\
\
Five-Times Sit-to-Stand.\
\
MINIMUM FUNCTIONAL DEMO\
\
1. User starts an assessment.\
2. Camera captures movements.\
3. ExecuTorch performs local model inference.\
4. System identifies sit-to-stand transitions.\
5. Application counts repetitions.\
6. Application measures completion time.\
7. Results appear on a dashboard.\
8. Results can be exported as structured data.\
\
OPTIONAL ENHANCEMENTS\
\
- Individual rise and descent times\
- Movement consistency measures\
- Quality-control flags\
- Comparison against reference timing\
- A second functional assessment\
\
CLINICAL TRIAL DEMONSTRATION\
\
Show a sample longitudinal patient profile.\
\
Use synthetic data for:\
\
- Baseline functional performance\
- Follow-up functional performance\
- GDF-15 concentrations\
- Body composition\
- Patient-reported physical functioning\
\
Demonstrate how real camera-derived functional\
measurements could be integrated with other\
trial measurements.\
\
Do not present synthetic measurements as real\
patient data.\
\
Technical deliverables should include:\
\
- Hardware and software requirements\
- Selected model and architecture\
- Data processing pipeline\
- User interface requirements\
- Measurement algorithms\
- Structured data output specification\
- Quality-control procedures\
- Known limitations\
- Fallback strategy\
